rship (crew cooperation), but unfriendly (communication), eats unhealthily (maybe reliability? not directly). No explicit reliability, stress resilience.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best overall. Compare C vs B vs D vs A.\n\nC: strong reliability, decision, calm, attention. Communication issues but maybe less severe than B's nasty remarks? Egocentric may affect crew. Not willing to further education may affect adaptability.\n\nB: strong reliability, stress, technical (weather, computer), but communication issues are nasty remarks, uncooperative, pretentious. Weak memory for numbers may affect attention.\n\nD: strong problem solving, responsibility, attention, but moody, loner, hot temper, know-it-all. No explicit reliability.\n\nA: leadership, anticipation, technical, but unfriendly, no reliability evidence.\n\nThus likely C or B. Which is stronger? The panel currently has leading candidate C per Agent 1. I could either agree, or propose D as alternative, or argue that B's issues are more severe, making C still best. Or I could bring up D's responsibility and problem solving as strengths, but his interpersonal issues may be severe.\n\nGiven the criteria, reliability is paramount. C is 100% reliable. B is conscientious but not explicitly 100% reliable. So C's reliability is a strong point. Decision quality and calm under pressure also strong. Communication issues are concerning but can be mitigated. B's nasty remarks are more severe. So I might agree with C.\n\nThus my vote: Candidate C.\n\nIn my public message, I should reference Agent 1's points, maybe add additional evidence about Candidate D or A to show I've considered them, but still support C. I can mention that D lacks explicit reliability evidence, and A lacks reliability and stress evidence, making C the best.\n\nThus produce public message: I agree with Agent 1, recommend Candidate C, citing reliability, decision quality, calmness, positive crew atmosphere, and note that while communication issues